@title Lantern Notes 3.8.0
@subtitle Released 2026-10-14
@date 2026-10-14

Shared folders, scheduled dark mode, Evernote import, faster search and a stack of fixes. Here is what changed.

## New

- **Shared folders.** Invite up to 25 collaborators to a folder and choose view or edit access for each person.
- **Scheduled dark mode.** Dark mode can now follow sunset, or a time range you set.
- **Import from Evernote.** Bring in your ENEX files, including attachments up to 50 MB each.

## Improved

- **Search is about twice as fast.** On a library of 10,000 notes, the median query dropped from 410 ms to 190 ms.
- **Better battery life on Android.** Background sync uses about 18 percent less battery.

## Fixed

- Tables keep their column widths when exported to PDF.
- The app no longer freezes when you open a note with more than 200 images.
- Reminders fire at the right time after a daylight saving change.
- Pasted web links keep their titles.
- On Windows, dragging a note onto a folder in the sidebar now works with a trackpad.
- The word count now includes text inside tables.

## Known issues

- Shared folders can't be used with end-to-end encrypted notebooks yet. Support is planned for 3.9.
- Evernote import drops nested tags deeper than three levels.

## Deprecations

!! Windows 8.1 support ends on 2027-01-31.
!! From version 3.9, Lantern Notes on Android needs Android 10 or later.
